#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# heaviside_theta

#% text
# `heaviside_theta(x)` gives 1 for x > 0 and 0 for x < 0.

#% text
# `heaviside_theta(x, y, ...)` gives the product.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At an exact 0 and for symbols the call stays unevaluated (the value at 0 is not defined).

#% item
# Unlike `unit_step`, which is 1 at 0.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
heaviside_theta(1.0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
heaviside_theta(-2)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
heaviside_theta(0)
#% output
#= heaviside_theta(0)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
heaviside_theta(pi - 3, 2)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
heaviside_theta(x)
#% output
#= heaviside_theta(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `unit_step`, `dirac_delta`, `sign`
